  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1100 AM CDT Fri May 8 2026\n\nFor Sunday, a more substantial wave with a cold front will come \ndown in the broad eastern trough. This will set off showers and a\nfew storms, starting Sunday afternoon, but especially Sunday \nevening. PWATs and other parameters are not impressive, so we are\nnot looking for a lot of rain, and we do not expect severe storms. \nMost areas will have less than one quarter inch of rain. \n\nAfter the cold front passes Monday morning, dry and slightly\ncooler air will move in with upper 60s to mid 70s for Monday and\nTuesday. Another front will slide through the area late Tuesday \ninto Wednesday, giving a low chance for showers and keeping our\nhighs mostly in the pleasant, seasonable 70s. Heading into next\nweekend, it looks like temps will creep upward into the 80s as the\nwestern ridge begins to expand eastward.",
